Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Owner feedback (screenshot: agent proposed 'a daily Hermes cron job' with
emoji bullet points):
- DEFAULT_SOUL_MD + DEFAULT_AGENT_IDENTITY gain two style rules: Nemesis is
  the only name (Hermes = runtime-internal, never in conversation) and no
  emojis/decorative symbols unless the student asks.
- Previous field-neutral SOUL added to _LEGACY_TEMPLATE_SOULS so app-written
  installs upgrade in place on next backend start (user-edited SOULs never
  touched).
- HERMES_AGENT_HELP_GUIDANCE rewritten: runtime attribution stays, but the
  agent must not present features as Hermes or send students to Hermes docs.
- Desktop-app interface line + steer-channel note rebranded.
- Live recorder copilot prompt: plain text only, no emojis.
- test_empty_dir_loads_seeded_global_soul expectation updated to the Nemesis
  persona (stale since the beta.5 rebrand).
